# Project conventions

## Stack
- **Vite + vanilla TypeScript.** No React/Vue/Svelte/Angular and no heavy UI kits. Small DOM helpers in `src/lib` are fine.
- **KaTeX** for math (`$...$` inline, `$$...$$` display). Bundle it locally so the app works offline. No CDN.
- **PWA**: manifest + service worker (`vite-plugin-pwa`, `registerType: 'prompt'`). Core flows work offline; LLM features need network and a key (with clipboard/Grok fallbacks).
- **Static only**: deployed to GitHub Pages (repo `xgrybvo6508-dot/learning-hub`). Vite `base: '/learning-hub/'`. Every asset URL, manifest `start_url`/`scope` and SW scope must respect this base. Use `import.meta.env.BASE_URL`, not hard-coded `/`.
- Tooling: `vitest` + `happy-dom` + `fake-indexeddb`, `eslint` (typescript-eslint), `prettier`, `tsx`, `@playwright/test` for e2e. Node ≥ 20.19.

## Folder layout
```
src/
  main.ts              # bootstrap only
  lib/                 # pure helpers: guards, result, time, dom, markdown, KaTeX, ids
  memory/              # IndexedDB + localStorage adapters, versioned schema, migrations, SRS, interleaving picker
  agent/               # OpenAI-compatible client, settings, errors, extract-json, validators
  agent/prompts/       # prompt templates imported with ?raw (e.g. mindmap-skill.md)
  modules/
    mistakes/          # (a) mistake log + SM-2 re-check queue
    courses/           # (b) course organizer + session log
    mindmap/           # (c) mindmapping trainer (vision feedback)
    voice/             # (d) voice window + structure-it LLM
    anki/              # (e) deck generator + .apkg export
    feynman/           # (f) Feynman-check agent (no lecturing)
    interleave/        # (g) daily interleaving scheduler
  ui/                  # views, components, CSS (see 30-design-system.mdc)
content/
  courses/             # bundled course Markdown (copied at build from learning-system when present)
```
Tests are colocated as `*.test.ts` next to the module.

## Code style
- `tsconfig`: `"strict": true`, `noUncheckedIndexedAccess`, `exactOptionalPropertyTypes`, `noImplicitOverride`. No `any`. Use `unknown` + type guards at boundaries (API responses, localStorage, LLM JSON).
- **Small pure modules.** Logic in `agent/`, `memory/`, `lib/`, `modules/**` core logic is pure and DOM-free where possible so it can be unit-tested. Side effects (fetch, storage, DOM) sit behind thin adapters that get injected.
- ES modules and named exports. One responsibility per file, roughly under 200 lines.
- Persisted data has a `version` field and a migration function. Never silently drop user memory.
- Errors are typed (`Result`-style or custom `Error` subclasses) and reach the UI as calm, plain-English messages.

## Testing
- vitest covers SRS scheduling, interleaving picker, storage migrations, every LLM JSON validator, prompt builders, and module-specific logic (see `docs/private/BRIEF.md` §4 acceptance criteria).
- Use a fake clock, fake storage and mocked `fetch`. No real network in unit tests.

## npm scripts (keep these names)
| script | command |
|---|---|
| `dev` | `vite` |
| `build` | `tsc --noEmit && vite build` |
| `preview` | `vite preview` |
| `test` | `vitest run` |
| `lint` | `eslint .` |
| `typecheck` | `tsc --noEmit` |
| `format` | `prettier --write .` |

Before declaring work done, run: `npm run typecheck && npm run lint && npm test && npm run build`.
